From: Xperia Hikari Linux Project <hikari-linux@localhost>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: use the V2 controller for command DMA

The V2 DSI command DMA engine is the bus master consuming this buffer.  Using
the DRM/MDP device for dma_alloc_coherent() can return an address translated
through the MDP IOMMU.  That IOVA is not usable by the separate MSM8x60 DSI
DMA master: on Hikari the programmed 0x7bc41000 address never completed a
command, while the DSI trigger remained asserted and IRQ 114 stayed at zero.

Allocate and free the V2 command buffer against the DSI platform device so
the DMA API returns an address in the DSI controller's DMA domain.

Signed-off-by: Xperia Hikari Linux Project <hikari-linux@localhost>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -1381,9 +1381,9 @@ int dsi_tx_buf_alloc_6g(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host, int size)
 
 int dsi_tx_buf_alloc_v2(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host, int size)
 {
-	struct drm_device *dev = msm_host->dev;
+	struct device *dev = &msm_host->pdev->dev;
 
-	msm_host->tx_buf = dma_alloc_coherent(dev->dev, size,
+	msm_host->tx_buf = dma_alloc_coherent(dev, size,
 					&msm_host->tx_buf_paddr, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!msm_host->tx_buf)
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -1415,7 +1415,7 @@ void msm_dsi_tx_buf_free(struct mipi_dsi_host *host)
 	}
 
 	if (msm_host->tx_buf)
-		dma_free_coherent(dev->dev, msm_host->tx_size, msm_host->tx_buf,
-			msm_host->tx_buf_paddr);
+		dma_free_coherent(&msm_host->pdev->dev, msm_host->tx_size,
+			msm_host->tx_buf,
 			msm_host->tx_buf_paddr);
 }
